{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrwxZGMKCSEZEyhjn7bC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed all three root causes in `name_key` in `contacts/dedupe.py`. The test now passes, and so do two extra checks I ran by hand.\n\n1. **Accents:** a hard-coded list of 8 accented characters was being stripped, so anything else (like `ç` or `ø`) slipped through. It now decomposes each name with Unicode NFKD and removes all combining marks.\n2. **Mac vs. Windows:** Mac usually types `é` as `e` plus a combining accent, and Windows as one character. The old code treated those as different names. The NFKD step makes both forms identical.\n3. **`ß` vs `ss`:** `.lower()` leaves `ß` as it is. I switched to `.casefold()`, which turns `ß` into `ss`.\n\nI also changed `email_key` to use `casefold()`, and whitespace is now collapsed after normalization. The first-seen record still survives, because I didn't touch the `dedupe` loop.\n\nThe two extra checks were `Straße` against `STRASSE`, and the combining-accent form `Jose\\u0301  Nu\\u0308` against `José Nü`. I didn't add them to the test file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4013,"cache_read_input_tokens":26664,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4013},"output_tokens":383,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d1887745-d9a1-4607-96a0-55eda4ac8480","uuid":"ed6720f1-2a4b-426b-aea0-f8a00b7de15a","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:05:17.518Z","request_id":"req_011CfrwxYhcpDXMAzc9SdUH5"}
